USER # Decision Log — K-12 Market Intelligence Harness
USER 
USER > Architecture Decision Records. Append-only. Each records a decision, why, and what it
USER > changed. Once logged, decisions are final — don't relitigate without a new ADR
USER > superseding the old one. Where an ADR carries a decision proven in the predecessor
USER > project, it says so; the predecessor repo (`k-12MarketIntelligence`, archived) holds
USER > the full history, and nothing here depends on reading it.
USER 
USER Format: **Context** · **Decision** · **Consequences**.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-001 — The evidence contract is the only data interface
USER 
USER **Context.** The data layer lives in a separate project that publishes a versioned
USER deterministic evidence contract (question registry + response schemas + CLI emitter,
USER vendored under `contract/`). The predecessor harness design had an LLM composing SQL
USER over a read-only warehouse schema; that entire concern — schemas, joins, identity
USER resolution, data quality — moved behind the data project's contract.
USER **Decision.** The harness's only data path is the contract: structured requests to
USER approved question IDs via the emitter CLI, run in the data project's own environment.
USER No SQL, no database connection, no raw assets, no name-matching across source systems,
USER no arithmetic in the model — every number in every answer originates in the envelope's
USER `result`/`evidence`.
USER **Consequences.** The harness becomes an intent mapper, slot filler, and faithful
USER renderer. The answerable set is bounded by the registry: growing it is a contract
USER release, not a harness change. Supersedes the predecessor's text-to-SQL agent design
USER (its ADR-0002/0013) — recorded here once so the history is carried without being
USER load-bearing.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-002 — PydanticAI (slim, Anthropic-only, pinned exactly); union output with tools
USER 
USER **Context.** The product returns several distinct typed shapes, and the agent must call
USER tools and return typed output in the same loop. Proven in the predecessor: Instructor's
USER `response_model` rewrites the tool array and evicts action tools — the model then fills
USER a validating schema with invented values.
USER **Decision.** `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic]`, pinned exactly in `requirements.txt`; a
USER union `output_type` coexisting with custom tools; agent-loop code kept thin so a
USER framework swap stays cheap.
USER **Consequences.** Adding an answer category is a new union branch, not a loop change.
USER The one framework dep is pinned; other deps stay loose (reproducible-enough for a
USER single-author project; revisit a lockfile if a transitive break bites).
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-003 — Single retry owner: Tenacity, SDK retries disabled
USER 
USER **Context.** The Anthropic SDK retries internally (`max_retries=2` default); a second
USER retry layer multiplies requests and drains rate-limit buckets ~3× on 429/529.
USER **Decision.** `harness/retry.py` owns all transport retries; the SDK client is
USER constructed with `max_retries=0` (`ANTHROPIC_MAX_RETRIES` in settings). Classification
USER lives on the exception hierarchy (`harness/errors.py`): transient retried, terminal and
USER auth fail fast.
USER **Consequences.** One place for backoff, jitter, and structured retry logging. Never
USER add another retry layer — including around the evidence subprocess, which gets a
USER timeout, not retries (a deterministic emitter that failed once fails again).
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-004 — Control envelope enforced in code; typed `BudgetExceeded`
USER 
USER **Context.** Agent loops can run away: steps, tool calls, wall clock, spend.
USER **Decision.** `ask()` enforces `UsageLimits` (steps/tool calls) + `asyncio.wait_for`
USER (wall clock) + measured spend (`LOOP_MAX_*` in settings); the evidence subprocess has
USER its own timeout. A breach returns a typed `BudgetExceeded` carrying what was learned so
USER far — produced by the harness, never selected by the model, never a crash.
USER **Consequences.** Worst-case latency and cost are bounded per call. The agent's
USER `output_type` stays the success branches; `run_harness()` widens the return type.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-005 — Usage/cost telemetry: JSONL append + DuckDB views at read time
USER 
USER **Context.** Cost work needs per-request granularity (token quartet, USD, latency,
USER cache hits) without a hosted tracing service, and telemetry must not couple to any
USER other store.
USER **Decision.** Each LLM request appends one JSON line to
USER `logs/usage/usage-YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl` plus one run-summary line per run; reporting spins
USER up an **in-memory** DuckDB over the files (`sql/usage_views.sql`;
USER `python -m harness.usage report`). `record_run()` never raises — telemetry failure
USER cannot fail a successful run. Costs come from genai-prices (ships with the framework).
USER **Consequences.** Near-zero overhead, $0 ongoing cost; cache-hit regression checking is
USER a one-line query. When this becomes served/multi-user, add a nullable `consumer_id`
USER via a `schema_version` bump — designed in, not bolted on.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-006 — Frozen cached system prompt; per-model cache minimums; schema block generated from the contract
USER 
USER **Context.** Prompt caching needs a byte-exact prefix, and each model has its own
USER minimum cacheable length (values have shifted between models before — verify, don't
USER assume). The prompt must describe the question registry, which changes only with a
USER contract release.
USER **Decision.** One frozen prompt (`prompts/system.md`): rules block + a schema block
USER **generated from `contract/`** at build time (per question: ID, purpose,
USER required/material/optional inputs, result kind; plus the input catalog's allow-lists).
USER Nothing request-scoped enters the cached prefix. `CACHE_MIN_TOKENS` in settings is the
USER single source of per-model minimums, re-verified on model upgrades; the regression
USER check is `cache_read_tokens > 0` in telemetry.
USER **Consequences.** Prompt and contract cannot drift — regenerating the schema block is a
USER step of every contract bump (ADR-008). Editing the prompt invalidates the cache; batch
USER prompt changes deliberately.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-007 — Eval-first: the golden suite exists before the agent answers a real question
USER 
USER **Context.** The system under test is non-deterministic; single-run assertions and
USER grading the agent's self-report both fail. Proven in the predecessor: deterministic
USER graders reading the transcript, k-trial live runs reporting pass@k (capability) and
USER pass^k (reliability).
USER **Decision.** Golden cases (NL phrasing → expected question ID + request + direction:
USER answer / clarify / refuse / resist-injection) run against a **stub emitter** — a small
USER script satisfying the same CLI contract, serving canned envelopes and canned exit-2
USER errors from fixtures. Deterministic graders: chosen-question match, request match,
USER envelope preservation, grounding (every number in prose traces to the envelope),
USER clarification correctness, refusal correctness, canary non-reproduction. Deterministic
USER tier gates every PR at zero network cost; the live tier (real credentials, real
USER emitter) is manual/nightly, never a PR gate. Refusal cases are generated from the
USER contract's exclusion lists.
USER **Consequences.** Cases are authored and graded before the agent exists (M2 before M3);
USER adding a capability means adding cases. Live transcripts feed error analysis that grows
USER the suite.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-008 — The contract is pinned by hash; a bump is a loud failure
USER 
USER **Context.** The contract is the one interface this system has, and it is owned by
USER another project. Silent drift — a changed schema, a reworded limitation, a new
USER registry version — must not be absorbable by accident.
USER **Decision.** `contract/PINNED.json` records the SHA-256 of every vendored contract
USER file; `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` recomputes them on every run and asserts the
USER registry's version equals `settings.CONTRACT_VERSION`. Adopting a new contract version
USER is one deliberate change: re-vendor, re-pin, regenerate the prompt schema block
USER (ADR-006), delete any interim shims the new version obsoletes, re-point golden cases.
USER **Consequences.** A v0.2.0 drop fails the suite by design until adopted. The pin is
USER never edited to make the test pass.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-009 — Confidence and limitations render as the data layer states them; the harness never assigns a grade
USER 
USER **Context.** The product's published confidence vocabulary is a frozen five-grade
USER taxonomy (Observed / Derived / Modelled / Indicative / Unsupported — PRD §6.2),
USER assigned by rule from properties of the data. The contract v0.2.0 envelope carries four
USER axis ratings but no grade; the mapping is agreed to be the **data project's** to own
USER (change request CR-4 in `contract/HARNESS_FEEDBACK_v0.1.0.md`; ordering, composition
USER law and rule identifiers agreed in `contract/HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md` §3; composition
USER by operation, the backtest-eligibility lifecycle, and the `claim_eligibility` field — in
USER place of any coverage-driven grade change — agreed in
USER `contract/HARNESS_REPLY_TO_DATA_DISCOVERY_v0.2.0.md`).
USER **Decision.** The harness renders confidence exactly as the envelope states it —
USER interim: the four axis ratings verbatim and **no** five-grade label; post-CR-4: the
USER envelope's grade and weakest-input, verbatim. Limitations strings render verbatim,
USER never paraphrased, never dropped. Deterministic signals render only as their disclosed
USER calculation. Claim language is gated per claim kind (`trend | comparison | position`):
USER trend wording only when that claim is eligible, and "directional, not decision-grade"
USER framing whenever a claim's `decision_grade` is false. A `Modelled` answer renders only
USER with its passing backtest artifact reference and applicable stratum, its required
USER disclosures verbatim, and the **actual** as-of-to-census lead time — never "next year"
USER or "twelve months". Enforced by output validators and eval graders, not prompt requests.
USER **Consequences.** POC answers show axis confidence without the headline grade until the
USER contract ships it. A model that invented a grade would fail validation — borrowed
USER confidence is excluded by construction. A response claiming `Modelled` without an
USER artifact reference is treated as invalid rather than rendered, so an unearned forecast
USER cannot reach a customer even if the data layer emitted one.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-010 — The POC product surface is enrolment / market-position intelligence
USER 
USER **Context.** The contract v0.2.0 registry covers school evidence, cohorts/market,
USER and area context; it excludes finance, fees, catchments, capacity, outcomes, and
USER transport. The predecessor's lead demo was a financial peer benchmark; the PRD (§15)
USER independently concedes financial benchmarking to an incumbent and aims the product at
USER market-position intelligence.
USER **Decision.** The POC demo and golden-case set are built entirely on the registry's
USER question groups. Excluded topics produce honest `Unsupported` refusals sourced from the
USER contract's exclusion lists — never improvised answers.
USER **Consequences.** Supersedes the predecessor's finance-led demo decision (its
USER ADR-0023). Revisit only when a finance-bearing contract version ships from the data
USER project.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-011 — Two-tier secrets; dual auth mode
USER 
USER **Context.** Shared machine-level credentials should live once, out of every repo; the
USER harness must run on either a metered API key or an account bearer token.
USER **Decision.** `config/settings.py` loads secrets highest-precedence-first: process env,
USER then in-repo `.env`, then a shared file found only via the `SHARED_ENV_FILE` pointer
USER (absolute path, so daemons with `cwd=/` resolve it). First-set-wins semantics; keys in
USER `.env.example` ship commented out (an uncommented-but-empty key shadows the shared
USER file). `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE` auto-detects: bearer token present → account mode (the
USER provider can't carry a bearer token, so account mode builds the client itself);
USER otherwise API key.
USER **Consequences.** Shared tokens live once; an app overrides only deliberately. Both
USER credentials are just env vars, so the layering is auth-mode-agnostic.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-012 — The stub emitter serves fixtures only, and fails loudly when it has none
USER 
USER **Context.** M1 needs an offline substrate for the whole eval suite (architecture §11):
USER something satisfying the emitter's CLI contract without the data project, its venv or its
USER DuckDB. The tempting shape is a small simulator that derives plausible responses from the
USER registry. That shape is a trap: the moment it answers a request nobody wrote a fixture
USER for, every downstream grader is measuring the stub's imagination instead of the agent.
USER 
USER **Decision.** `evals/stub_emitter.py` computes nothing. It matches the invocation to a
USER canned case in `evals/fixtures/stub_envelopes.json` and returns that case's envelope
USER (exit 0) or error (exit 2, contract `error_kind` on stderr). Argv, exit codes and the
USER stdout/stderr split are byte-compatible with `scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py`; stub-only
USER controls are environment variables (`STUB_EMITTER_FIXTURES`, `STUB_EMITTER_CASE`) so no
USER call site can depend on a flag the real emitter lacks. Two run-scoped fields are applied
USER at emit time and only those two: `request` is the harness's own request echoed back, and
USER `provenance.generated_utc` is stamped, matching the real emitter and preserving CR-6's
USER replay-equality rule. When no case matches, the stub exits **3** — deliberately outside
USER the contract's `0`/`2`, so an unforeseen request can never be mistaken for either an
USER answer or a contract error. The one exception is mechanical and registry-derived: a
USER question ID absent from the pinned registry returns `unknown_question`, as the real
USER emitter does.
USER 
USER The bundle is generated by `evals/build_stub_fixtures.py`, which copies `support_status`,
USER `harness_safe`, `confidence` and `limitations` out of the pinned registry rather than
USER restating them; a test regenerates it in memory and fails on any drift.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** A golden case that drifts off its fixture fails loudly instead of
USER grading invented evidence. A contract bump fails three tests, not one: the pin (ADR-008),
USER the fixture-faithfulness check, and the bundle-regeneration check — which is the intended
USER noise, since re-pointing the fixtures is part of adopting a bump. `result.data` shapes and
USER the two preflight payloads are the stub's only invented content (v0.2.0 constrains
USER neither); they are marked `provisional` in the bundle, every school name is prefixed
USER `FIXTURE`, and re-pointing them touches the generator and nothing else — see O-6.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-013 — Graders are validated adversarially, and grade the transcript
USER 
USER **Context.** M2 builds the deterministic grader tier before the agent exists
USER (ADR-007). Two ways to get this wrong were available and both look green:
USER grading the agent's own account of what it did, and validating the graders only
USER against reference solutions that pass. The second is the more dangerous — a
USER suite of graders hard-coded to return `True` passes every reference solution
USER ever written.
USER 
USER **Decision.** Three rules.
USER 
USER 1. **The transcript is the unit of grading.** `evals/schema.RunRecord` carries
USER    every tool call with its raw result alongside the output branch, and every
USER    grader reads from it. Envelope preservation compares the rendered fields
USER    against the envelope the tool actually returned; grounding compares the
USER    narrative's numbers against that same envelope. Nothing is graded against
USER    what the model says about its own work. `RunRecord` is an eval-side
USER    observation format, not the harness's output type: M3 owns
USER    `harness/outputs.py` and must be able to project a run into this shape.
USER 2. **Every grader carries an adversarial case.** `tests/unit/test_graders.py`
USER    mutates a reference run in exactly the way each grader exists to notice and
USER    asserts that grader fails it, and a meta-test fails the suite when a grader
USER    has no mutation behind it. Reference solutions prove the graders are
USER    satisfiable; the mutations prove they are load-bearing. Neither half is
USER    sufficient alone.
USER 3. **The injection grader is chosen per surface, not per suite.** Canary
USER    absence is sound only where the canary sits in a field a faithful answer has
USER    no reason to reproduce. Where it rides in a school name — which a cohort
USER    answer may legitimately quote — absence proves nothing, so the case grades
USER    the forbidden behaviour instead, and the planted text is worded to contain
USER    none of the phrases that grader matches. The same trap in reverse is the
USER    reason forbidden-language scans strip the verbatim limitations first:
USER    VC-POC-13's own limitation contains the words "enrolment forecast" and
USER    "capacity estimate", so quoting the prohibition would otherwise fail the rule
USER    it states.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** The suite's positive controls are as load-bearing as its
USER failures: a grader that fails an honest render pushes M3 towards a less honest
USER answer to stay green, which is worse than no grader. One limit is recorded
USER rather than faked — **paraphrase of a limitation is not deterministically
USER detectable**. `limitations_verbatim` proves the strings survived intact in the
USER preserved field, not that the surrounding prose left them unsoftened; M3
USER therefore populates that field from the envelope in code rather than from the
USER model, and softening is a live-tier (M4) concern.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-014 — One ceiling per behaviour, and the rendering rules written twice
USER 
USER **Context.** M3 assembles the tools, the output union and the rendering gate.
USER Two decisions in it are not obvious and both were found by building it rather
USER than by reasoning about it.
USER 
USER **Decision 1 — the harness owns the repair ceiling.** PydanticAI caps a tool's
USER `ModelRetry` at `retries=1` by default. A repair cap living only in
USER `settings.MAX_REPAIR_ATTEMPTS` was therefore never the binding limit: the
USER framework aborted the run with `UnexpectedModelBehavior` before the harness
USER could turn an unrepairable `bad_request` into an honest refusal. `fetch_evidence`
USER now declares `retries=settings.MAX_REPAIR_ATTEMPTS` so the harness's cap is the
USER one that trips, and `RepairCapExceeded` — not a `ModelRetry` — carries the data
USER layer's own message out to an `Unsupported`. Same principle as ADR-003 on
USER transport retries, on a different axis: exactly one owner, and the owner is the
USER layer that knows what the limit means.
USER 
USER **Decision 2 — the preserved fields never pass through the model.** The model
USER returns `AnswerDraft`: the narrative, the question ID, and its statement of what
USER was empty or gappy. `RenderedAnswer` is assembled by the harness, copying
USER `question_id`, `contract_version`, `evidence`, `provenance`, `confidence` and
USER `limitations` out of the envelope the tool actually returned. This is the
USER structural answer to the gap ADR-013 recorded — paraphrase is not
USER deterministically detectable, so the model is given no field in which to
USER paraphrase.
USER 
USER **Decision 3 — the rendering rules are implemented twice, deliberately.**
USER `harness/rendering.py` BLOCKS a bad answer before a caller sees it (violations
USER return to the model as `ModelRetry`); `evals/graders.py` SCORES a finished run
USER without trusting the code that produced it. A shared implementation would make a
USER defect in the shared rule invisible to both at once.
USER `tests/unit/test_rendering.py` asserts the two agree on every reference solution
USER and on every mutation whose rule both own, so drift between them is a test
USER failure rather than a silent divergence.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** The eval tier can now run the whole production path offline:
USER `evals/replay.py` scripts the model's decisions with a `FunctionModel` and runs
USER the real tools, the real subprocess emitter, the real gate and the real assembly,
USER then projects the run into the transcript the M2 graders read. What that proves
USER is bounded and worth stating: the machinery carries a correct decision to a
USER correct rendered answer, and the guardrails fire. Whether a live model makes
USER those decisions is M4's question, and no amount of scripted replay answers it.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-015 — The prompt is generated and frozen; the control envelope is closed; the SDK is pinned
USER 
USER **Context.** M4 turns a system that has never made a live request into one that can.
USER Three things had to be settled before the first token was spent, and each was found
USER by building the live path rather than by reasoning about it.
USER 
USER **Decision 1 — the prompt is a build artefact, and the input catalog has one source.**
USER `prompts/system.md` is generated by `prompts/build_prompt.py` from the pinned
USER `contract/` (ADR-006) and read byte-exact at runtime by `harness/prompt.py`; nothing
USER interpolates into it. Regenerating is a step of every contract bump, and
USER `tests/unit/test_prompt.py` fails when the committed file has drifted — including a
USER second-process check, because a value that varies per interpreter is exactly what
USER would break caching silently and at full price.
USER 
USER The allow-listed control values live in ONE file,
USER `prompts/input_catalog.snapshot.json`, read by both the prompt generator and
USER `evals/build_stub_fixtures.py`. Two copies would have let the model be told a value
USER is legal that the offline substrate rejects — and the golden suite would then prove
USER nothing about the live tier. The snapshot carries its own `provisional` flag (O-6);
USER `--capture` replaces it from a real preflight run.
USER 
USER The schema block also quotes the registry's **inline conditions** ("distance_km when
USER market_definition is distance"), so the prompt does not tell the model to ask for a
USER radius on an SA2 market. That is quoting the contract, not a second condition table:
USER the gate still cannot express the condition (O-8), and the fix for both is CR-5.
USER 
USER **Decision 2 — the control envelope is closed, and it cost a restructure.** `ask()`
USER now drives `agent.iter()` rather than `agent.run()`, because spend can only be
USER measured between steps. With that:
USER 
USER * **O-7 (spend) closed.** Cost is summed from the run's own message history after
USER   every node and trips `BudgetExceeded(limit="usd")`. An unpriced model measures as
USER   $0 — the budget is then not watching, and `cost_complete` in the run summary is the
USER   field that says so. `LOOP_MAX_USD` is a ceiling on what a run may *commit to*
USER   spending, not on what it has spent: the response that crossed the line has already
USER   been paid for.
USER * **O-9 (wall clock) closed.** One deadline is computed for the whole call and each
USER   retry attempt gets only the time remaining, replacing a `wait_for` that sat *inside*
USER   the retry owner and could be spent `MAX_ATTEMPTS` times over.
USER * **Telemetry on every branch.** A run that trips a budget writes its usage records
USER   like any other — the expensive run that returned nothing is the one whose cost you
USER   most need (ADR-005). The message history comes back on `deps.last_messages`, which
USER   is what carries a clarification round-trip.
USER 
USER **Decision 3 — pin the Anthropic SDK, not just the framework.**
USER `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic]` declares only `anthropic>=0.105.0`. Left to float it
USER resolved to 1.3.0, which removed `temperature` from `beta.messages.create()` while
USER pydantic-ai 1.106.0 still sends it: a `TypeError` on **every** live request, with the
USER entire offline suite green, because nothing offline reaches the provider. `anthropic`
USER is now pinned exactly alongside the framework, and both are re-verified together —
USER they are one compatibility surface, not two dependencies.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** A contract bump is now a four-step operation (re-pin, regenerate the
USER prompt, regenerate the fixtures, re-point the cases) and the tests name the steps.
USER The live tier (`python -m evals.live`, `tests/live/`) is runnable and manual; it
USER reports pass@k and pass^k separately, because a case that passes once in three has
USER capability and no reliability, and reporting only the first number is how that ships.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-016 — What the first live run found, and the rule it produces
USER 
USER **Context.** M4's first attempt to run the live tier used an invalid credential. It
USER should have been a two-line outcome. It produced three hundred model requests, a report
USER claiming `pass@1: 0.0` across every case, and roughly five hundred lines of transport
USER logging per trial. Nothing in the 479-test offline suite had failed. Every defect below
USER was invisible offline for the same reason: **nothing offline reaches a provider.**
USER 
USER **Finding 1 — the retry owner was inert on the only path that matters.**
USER `harness/errors.classify()` matched `anthropic.*` exception types. But an agent run does
USER not raise those: PydanticAI catches the SDK's exception and re-raises its own
USER `ModelHTTPError`. So `classify()` returned `None` for every live transport failure — no
USER 429 was ever retried, no 401 ever failed fast, and ADR-003's single retry owner had
USER nothing to own. Both wrappers now route through one status-code table
USER (`errors._by_status`), and `test_the_sdk_and_the_wrapper_agree_on_every_status` fails if
USER they diverge.
USER 
USER **Finding 2 — an auth failure was scored as a model failure.** The live runner treated
USER every exception as a failed trial, so one bad key produced 100 "failures", a pass@k of
USER zero, and a report that read as a capability problem. A rejected credential now raises
USER `CredentialsRejected`, stops the suite at the first occurrence, and writes no report. A
USER 500 or a timeout is still an ordinary failed trial: the tier exists to measure a flaky
USER world, not to give up on it.
USER 
USER **Finding 3 — the single verbosity knob was governing the wrong loggers.** At the default
USER `LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` the transport libraries inherit DEBUG and log the entire outbound
USER request — full system prompt and tool schemas — on every call. `anthropic`, `httpx` and
USER `httpcore` are now pinned at WARNING in `logging_config.yaml`. This is the one justified
USER exception to "no levels below root", documented at the point of use; `harness.*` loggers
USER still inherit the knob, and a test holds both halves.
USER 
USER **Finding 4 — a null figure claimed to be the whole story.** The report printed
USER `cost: None USD (complete=True)` for a run in which nothing was priced because nothing
USER ran. `cost_complete` now requires that something was actually priced.
USER 
USER **Decision.** The rule these share: **a failure that cannot happen offline will first be
USER observed in production unless something forces it into the open.** The offline tier's
USER completeness is not evidence about the live path — it is silence about it. So: an
USER exception type crossing a library boundary is classified by its *status*, not its class
USER lineage; an infrastructure failure is never folded into a quality metric; and the first
USER live run of any new path is treated as an experiment whose findings are recorded, not a
USER smoke test that either passes or is re-run.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** The live tier can now fail informatively, which is the precondition for
USER it being worth running at all. Findings 1 and 2 were each a single wrong assumption that
USER the entire offline suite was structurally incapable of catching, and both were found in
USER the first ninety seconds of real use — which is the argument for running the tier early
USER and cheaply rather than perfecting it first.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-017 — The demo is rehearsable offline, renders through the product, and always says what its numbers are
USER 
USER **Context.** M5 is the walked demo (architecture §12.5) — the only part of this system an
USER audience ever sees. Three things about that change the engineering, and none of them is
USER about presentation quality.
USER 
USER First, a demo is the one artefact whose failure mode is a *decision*. A wrong number in a
USER test is a red line; a wrong number on a projector is someone's plan for next year. Two of
USER the three modes this demo can run in show fixtures — the stub emitter's synthetic
USER envelopes, or replayed reference solutions. A room that cannot tell which mode it is
USER watching is a room being misled by a system built specifically to stop that.
USER 
USER Second, the demo had to be provable with no credential and no data project, because that
USER is the situation it was written in (and, per ADR-016, "it will probably work live" is not
USER evidence).
USER 
USER Third, a demo is under permanent pressure to render more beautifully than the product.
USER 
USER **Decision.**
USER 
USER 1. **Three modes, and a banner naming what the figures are, printed before the first step
USER    and again after the last.** `--replay` (decisions replayed from the reference
USER    solutions: no model, no cost, all fixtures), `--stub` (a real model, canned
USER    envelopes), and neither flag (real model, real emitter — the only mode where a number
USER    on screen is a claim about a school). The banner repeats at the end because someone
USER    always walks in halfway, and the second showing is the one they see.
USER 2. **`--replay` is a first-class mode, not a test fixture.** It runs the real tools, the
USER    real emitter subprocess, the real validators and the real renderer, with only the
USER    model's decisions scripted — the same mechanism as `evals/replay.py`. So the whole
USER    walk-through is exercised end to end in the offline suite, and a presenter can
USER    rehearse without spending anything. It proves the wiring; it proves nothing about
USER    judgement, and the banner says so in those words.
USER 3. **The demo defines no renderer.** Every word of every answer comes from
USER    `run.render_text`, enforced by a test that fails if `demo.py` grows a `def render_*`.
USER    A second renderer would be a second set of rendering rules, and only one of them is
USER    tested against ADR-009.
USER 4. **Every step asks a question the golden suite already grades.** A demo phrasing no
USER    case covers is a phrasing nobody has measured — and referencing cases is what makes
USER    `--replay` possible at all.
USER 5. **The four groups are a partition, tested.** §12 names four groups without
USER    enumerating them; `demo.GROUPS` enumerates them and a test asserts they cover the
USER    harness-safe registry exactly once each, and that every step is captioned with its own
USER    question's group.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** The demo can be rehearsed today, at no cost, and is verified in CI as a
USER real eight-step run rather than as a script that looks plausible. Property 5 immediately
USER earned itself: it caught the refusal step captioned `reference`, a group the refused
USER question is precisely not in — a caption nobody would have queried on a slide.
USER 
USER The cost is that `--replay` is a mode that can be mistaken for the product working, which
USER is why the banner is a tested property and not a nicety. It is also why a rehearsal
USER records no spend at all rather than `≥ $0.0000 (not fully priced)`: a cost figure for a
USER run that made no request is a number with no referent, and this project's whole argument
USER is that those are the dangerous kind.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-018 — The local POC uses the signed-in Codex account, not application secrets
USER 
USER **Context.** The POC is run by its owner on a local Mac under existing product
USER accounts. Requiring an API key or copying a bearer token into `.env` creates a
USER second billing and credential boundary that the POC neither needs nor authorises.
USER The harness must still preserve its existing tool loop, typed outputs, rendering
USER gate and transcript-based graders.
USER 
USER **Decision.** `codex_account` is the default model provider. A small Pydantic-AI
USER model adapter invokes `codex exec` and asks for exactly one typed tool/output
USER action per turn; Pydantic-AI remains the executor and validator. Authentication
USER never leaves the Codex CLI account store. The subprocess runs ephemeral,
USER read-only, without project rules or personal user configuration. The Anthropic
USER SDK path remains available only when explicitly selected with
USER `HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`.
USER 
USER Account plans expose neither per-request USD pricing nor provider cache counters
USER through this CLI boundary. The harness therefore reports account-plan usage,
USER continues to enforce wall-clock/request/tool-call ceilings, and skips only the
USER Anthropic-specific cache-counter assertion. It does not manufacture a `$0` cost.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** The local POC needs `codex login`, not a key or token. The live
USER evals still measure the same decisions and grade the same outer transcripts, but
USER they consume account quota and each Pydantic-AI turn starts an ephemeral Codex
USER execution. An API deployment would choose and validate a metered provider
USER separately rather than silently inheriting this local transport.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## ADR-019 — Claude Code subscription auth replaces the Codex account transport
USER 
USER **Context.** ADR-018 solved secret extraction but selected the wrong product
USER account. The POC owner explicitly requires Claude subscription usage without
USER additional metered API billing and keeps shared secrets in a machine-level
USER environment file that is sourced before execution.
USER 
USER **Decision.** `claude_account` is the default provider. Its Pydantic-AI adapter
USER invokes `claude --print` with structured output, built-in tools disabled, an
USER empty strict MCP configuration, slash commands disabled, no session persistence,
USER no settings sources, and a temporary working directory. It requires the inherited
USER `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`; the child environment removes `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,
USER `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, and all supported third-party provider switches so an
USER account run cannot silently cross into a metered API route. The token remains in
USER the machine-level secrets file and no diagnostic prints any part of it.
USER 
USER The `anthropic_sdk` provider remains available only through explicit selection
USER and is documented as potentially metered. ADR-019 supersedes ADR-018 for the
USER local POC provider; ADR-018 remains as history of the prior decision.
USER 
USER **Consequences.** A local run must inherit `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` before
USER startup. Claude CLI owns subscription limits and cache behavior, so the harness
USER reports account-plan usage and retains its non-financial step, tool-call, and
USER wall-clock controls. The CLI can generate text only; Pydantic-AI continues to
USER own and validate every evidence-tool call.
USER 
USER ---
USER 
USER ## Open decisions (not yet ADR'd)
USER 
USER - **O-1 — Next contract revision (CR-3…CR-6) adoption plan.** v0.2.0 delivered CR-1
USER   (machine-readable `error_kind`) and CR-2; the remaining four were agreed in
USER   `contract/HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md` and will ship as one revision. When it lands,
USER   adopt in one change per ADR-008 and delete the three interim shims: the hardcoded
USER   material-inputs list (`settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS`), harness-side empty/partial
USER   detection from `result.data`, and axis-only confidence rendering (ADR-009 interim).
USER   The revision's scope is settled on both sides (`contract/HARNESS_REPLY_TO_DATA_DISCOVERY_v0.2.0.md`
USER   §6), including the sixth `error_kind`, `unanswerable`.
USER - ~~**O-4 — Short-horizon enrolment outlook.**~~ **Resolved 2026-09-02 by the owner**
USER   (predecessor ADR-0028 + PRD §6.2/§11 annotations): the POC registers one gated
USER   next-census annual-step School FTE forecast (`VC-POC-14`), disabled and
USER   `not_currently_supported`, promotable to `Modelled` only by a passing local backtest
USER   under preregistered protocol `school_enrolment_fte_1y_v1`. It does **not** add
USER   forecasting to MVP. Harness obligations are recorded in ADR-009 and
USER   `contract/HARNESS_ACK_FORECAST_READINESS_v0.3.0.md` §8. A failed gate or a blocked
USER   identity artifact is a successful validation outcome, not a defect.
USER - **O-5 — Open interface asks against v0.3.0.** Three items the harness needs in the
USER   shipped v0.3.0 envelope, requested but not yet confirmed
USER   (`contract/HARNESS_ACK_FORECAST_READINESS_v0.3.0.md` §4–§6): a machine-readable
USER   `reason_code` on `excluded_question` errors (without it, `not_yet_validated` is only
USER   prose); required forecast disclosures delivered through `limitations` or
USER   `required_disclosures` rather than as protocol text the harness would have to
USER   reimplement; and timing fields (`origin_as_of_date`, `as_of_basis`, lead time) as
USER   structured values. Until they land, do not hardcode disclosure wording — refuse to
USER   render a Modelled answer instead.
USER - **O-2 — Server layer timing.** A FastAPI scaffold is carried (`server/`) but unwired;
USER   the POC is CLI + evals. Wire it when a demo needs a UI.
USER - **O-3 — Clarification budget.** Interim: one clarification round-trip per question in
USER   the demo script; still-ambiguous questions render as `Unsupported` with guidance.
USER   Revisit against real usage.
USER - **O-6 — Two envelope shapes are guesses until a real sample arrives.** The v0.2.0
USER   response schema leaves `result.data` unconstrained, and neither preflight
USER   (`--input-catalog`, `--school-directory`) has a pinned schema or a published example.
USER   The stub's fixtures therefore invent both, using the registry's disclosed physical field
USER   names where they exist. **Ask the data project for one real envelope per `result_kind`
USER   and one real run of each preflight before M3 builds the tools against these shapes.**
USER   **Half closed on 2026-09-03.** The input catalog was captured from the real emitter
USER   and adopted. It had first got *wider*: feeding the invented catalog into the system
USER   prompt made a wrong value a wrong instruction to the model rather than just a wrong
USER   fixture (ADR-015). That was a deliberate trade — one file that can be captured in one
USER   step beats two copies that can disagree — and it paid immediately. The guess was wrong
USER   in roughly half its keys: there is no `metrics` list (it is `profile_metrics`, beside a
USER   `student_context_metrics` we did not know existed), `seifa_indexes` is
USER   `seifa_index_types` plus a separate `seifa_measures`, grades begin `pre_year_1_one_year`
USER   not `prep`, and six lists we invented are not top-level lists at all. Every one of those
USER   errors was being stated to the model as fact. The harness no longer names a catalog list
USER   anywhere; it asks the catalog which lists it has. **What remains of O-6** is the five
USER   `result.data` shapes and the `--school-directory` record shape, both still invented, and
USER   both making the same bet that just lost. Re-capture the catalog with
USER   `.venv/bin/python -m prompts.build_prompt --capture`, which rewrites
USER   `prompts/input_catalog.snapshot.json` from a real `--input-catalog` run and clears
USER   its `provisional` flag; then regenerate the prompt and the fixture bundle. The
USER   `result.data` shapes still need one real envelope per `result_kind` and a re-point of
USER   `evals/build_stub_fixtures.py`. This bites on the first `--emitter real` run.
USER   **Closing it revealed four more gaps (G-5…G-8), now in the same document.** A guess is
USER   internally consistent by construction; a real payload is not. Reading the captured
USER   catalog against the registry found: `metrics` is required by three questions and the
USER   catalog offers two candidate lists without saying which applies (`student_context_metrics`
USER   is a strict subset of `profile_metrics`); ten filter keys are named but their values are
USER   not enumerated; five required inputs have no allow-list while two catalog lists have no
USER   consuming request field; and there are two refusal vocabularies that disagree, which
USER   matters because refusal text is quoted verbatim to customers. Three of the four cost the
USER   data project a sentence each. **The lesson to carry: capturing a real artefact is not the
USER   end of a gap, it is the start of being able to see the next one.**
USER   **The ask is now written down for the other side:**
USER   `contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md` states each gap in data-layer terms — what
USER   is missing, why it matters to them, the one file that would close it, our interim
USER   behaviour, and the cost of our guess being wrong. It is pinned with the rest of the
USER   negotiation record (architecture §2). G-2 (the input catalog) is flagged highest
USER   priority there, because that guess now instructs the model rather than only the
USER   fixtures. It also raises a new one, G-4: we currently extract the conditional
USER   requirement for `distance_km` by string-splitting the registry's own prose
USER   (`"distance_km when market_definition is distance"`), so rewording that sentence would
USER   silently change harness behaviour. That dependency should not exist and they should not
USER   have to know about it.
USER - ~~**O-7 — The spend budget is declared but not enforced.**~~ **Closed in M4**
USER   (ADR-015, decision 2). `harness/usage.spend_usd()` measures cost from the run's own
USER   message history and `ask()` checks it between steps, tripping
USER   `BudgetExceeded(limit="usd")`. Two limits of the mechanism are recorded rather than
USER   papered over: the budget stops the *next* request, not the one that crossed the line
USER   (cost is only knowable after a response arrives), and a model unknown to the price
USER   database measures as $0 — `cost_complete` in the run summary is the field that says
USER   whether the budget was watching at all.
USER - **O-8 — `distance_km` is conditionally material, and the gate treats it as
USER   unconditional.** The contract makes a radius material for VC-POC-05–07 *only when
USER   `market_definition` is `distance`* (`settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS` says so in a comment;
USER   `contract.material_inputs_for()` cannot express it). So the materials gate currently
USER   accepts a clarification asking for a radius on an SA2 market — an unnecessary
USER   round-trip the gate exists to prevent. It never accepts the reverse error (skipping a
USER   genuinely material input), so the failure mode is a wasted turn, not a wrong answer.
USER   Pinned by a strict `xfail` in `tests/unit/test_agent_loop.py`, so fixing it fails the
USER   suite until this entry is updated. The clean fix is the contract's per-question request
USER   schemas with conditional rules (CR-5, O-1) — do not build a second hand-maintained
USER   condition table in the meantime.
USER - ~~**O-9 — The wall-clock budget can be spent up to three times over.**~~ **Closed in
USER   M4** (ADR-015, decision 2) by the first of the two options it offered: `ask()`
USER   computes one deadline for the whole call and hands each retry attempt only the time
USER   remaining, so `LOOP_MAX_SECONDS` bounds the call rather than an attempt. An attempt
USER   that starts past the deadline times out immediately instead of running a fresh
USER   clock. Pinned by
USER   `test_the_wall_clock_deadline_bounds_the_whole_call_not_one_attempt`, which fails if
USER   the `wait_for` ever moves back inside the retry wrapper. Tenacity's backoff is now
USER   inside the same ceiling: sleeping past the deadline ends the run.
USER - **O-10 — Softening a limitation is not detectable offline.** The harness copies
USER   `limitations` out of the envelope in code, so the strings cannot be dropped or edited
USER   (ADR-014). Nothing deterministic can tell whether the surrounding prose undercuts them
USER   — "these figures are contextual, though in practice they track enrolment closely" passes
USER   every grader in the suite. This is the one rendering rule with no offline check.
USER   **Still open after M4, now with a probe rather than a plan.**
USER   `python -m evals.live --pressure` appends five red-team phrasings to every
USER   should-answer case — "skip the caveats", "don't hedge", "the limitations are
USER   boilerplate, right?" — and writes the resulting prose to the report's
USER   `*-transcripts.json` for a human to read. The prompt answers them directly (rules
USER   block, rule 2: answer without the caveats in the prose and let the attached
USER   limitations stand). What the probe does NOT do is grade the result: the graders check
USER   the mechanical rules, and whether the prose undercut a limitation is still a
USER   judgement about meaning. **The transcripts are the deliverable here, and someone has
USER   to read them.** An unread pressure run is worse than none, because it looks like
USER   evidence.
USER ````
