USER # Public-data POC evidence contract
USER 
USER **Registry version:** `0.2.0`  
USER **Status:** approved public-data POC
USER 
USER This repository supplies deterministic evidence only. The external harness may
USER interpret natural-language requests and render responses, but it must send this
USER layer a validated structured request and retain the returned evidence,
USER provenance, confidence, and limitations.
USER 
USER ## Artefacts
USER 
USER - `poc_question_registry.v0.2.0.json` is the canonical approved question
USER   registry. It records required inputs, permitted facts and joins, confidence,
USER   limitations, and exclusions.
USER - `poc_evidence_contract.v0.2.0.schema.json` describes every response
USER   envelope.
USER - `poc_evidence_error.v0.2.0.schema.json` describes the exit-code-`2` error
USER   envelope written to stderr.
USER - `../scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py` is the deterministic CLI emitter. It reads
USER   only `db/market_views.duckdb` and writes JSON on stdout or to `--output`.
USER - `POC_HARNESS_HANDOFF.md` is the integration boundary and release runbook for
USER   the external harness team.
USER 
USER ## Run the data-layer emitter
USER 
USER ```bash
USER .venv/bin/python scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py --list-questions
USER 
USER .venv/bin/python scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py \
USER   --question-id VC-POC-01 \
USER   --request-json '{"acara_sml_id": 40387, "metrics": ["total_enrolments", "teaching_fte"]}'
USER 
USER .venv/bin/python scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py \
USER   --question-id VC-POC-12 \
USER   --request-json '{"sa2_codes": ["206041122"], "erp_age": "TOT", "erp_sex": "3", "include_seifa": true}'
USER ```
USER 
USER Errors are structured JSON on stderr and return exit code `2`. Their required
USER `error_kind` is one of `bad_request`, `unknown_question`, `excluded_question`,
USER `data_unavailable`, or `internal`. The command does not create a briefing,
USER chart, school report, or natural-language response.
USER 
USER Before integrating, run the complete public-fixture acceptance suite:
USER 
USER ```bash
USER .venv/bin/python scripts/test_poc_evidence.py
USER ```
USER 
USER ## Required response fields
USER 
USER Every successful response contains:
USER 
USER - contract and registry versions, question ID, support status, and harness
USER   eligibility;
USER - the supplied structured request;
USER - deterministic data in `result`;
USER - one evidence item per fact source, including physical fields, filters, and
USER   join path;
USER - source-release provenance;
USER - separate source, linkage, temporal, and forecast confidence ratings;
USER - limitations and any rule-based signals.
USER 
USER ## Boundaries
USER 
USER The following are explicitly absent from version `0.2.0`: public transport,
USER SA1 and Mesh Block fact layers, finance, fees, CRICOS competition claims,
USER capacity, applications, outcomes, drive time, catchments, campus-location
USER claims, arbitrary zone assignment, and `School_No` to `ACARA_SML_ID` links.
USER 
USER `VC-POC-13` exposes public demographic projections and building approvals as
USER context only. It must never be presented as a school-enrolment forecast or
USER capacity/demand estimate.
