USER contract/POC_CONTRACT_V0.3_SPEC.md
USER ````
USER # POC evidence contract v0.3.0 implementation specification
USER 
USER **Status:** implemented — interface (JSON Schemas) complete; v0.3 emitter aligned\
USER **Machine-readable companion:** `catalogue/poc_contract_v0.3.0.draft.json`\
USER **JSON Schemas:** see [Interface design (v0.3 JSON Schemas)](#interface-design-v03-json-schemas)\
USER **Scope:** CR-3 through CR-6, error corrections, claim eligibility, and the gated forecast registration
USER 
USER ## Settled decisions
USER 
USER - `data_status` is structured per evidence/component and never infers causes.
USER - Per-question request schemas reject unknown fields and emit a complete
USER   `resolved_request`.
USER - Replay equality covers the entire semantic response except
USER   `provenance.generated_utc` within the same contract and data release.
USER - `unanswerable` is added to the error taxonomy.
USER - Excluded IDs and refusal reasons move into the registry.
USER - Grade is assigned by operation, capped by the weakest input, and owned by the
USER   data layer.
USER - Coverage affects claim eligibility, not the production grade of an observed
USER   figure.
USER - Backtest eligibility is separated from backtest execution state.
USER - The short-horizon forecast enters the registry disabled and can jump from
USER   `Unsupported` to `Modelled` only through a passing applicable local backtest.
USER 
USER ## Error boundary
USER 
USER | Kind | Mechanical test | Harness action |
USER | --- | --- | --- |
USER | `bad_request` | Harness can repair request syntax, shape, value, or directory identity | Repair and retry |
USER | `unknown_question` | ID absent from registry | Abstain |
USER | `excluded_question` | Registry contains an exclusion/refusal entry | Abstain with registry reason |
USER | `unanswerable` | Valid registered request; required fact value absent for these inputs | Abstain without retry |
USER | `data_unavailable` | Database or explicitly required table unavailable | Operational stop |
USER | `internal` | Unexpected implementation/query defect | Operational stop |
USER 
USER An `acara_sml_id` absent from the pinned directory is `bad_request`, because the
USER harness violated the selector obligation. A directory-valid record lacking a
USER coordinate or selected geography is `unanswerable`.
USER 
USER Every dispatch path declares and checks its required tables before executing.
USER Do not map every DuckDB catalogue exception to `data_unavailable`: an invalid
USER column or SQL defect is internal.
USER 
USER ## Successful envelope additions
USER 
USER Required in v0.3.0:
USER 
USER ```json
USER {
USER   "request": {},
USER   "resolved_request": {},
USER   "result": {},
USER   "data_status": {},
USER   "evidence": [],
USER   "provenance": {},
USER   "confidence": {"grade": {}},
USER   "claim_eligibility": {},
USER   "limitations": [],
USER   "deterministic_signals": []
USER }
USER ```
USER 
USER `request` is exactly what the harness supplied. `resolved_request` contains all
USER validated, defaulted and dynamically resolved values. Evidence filters must
USER agree with it.
USER 
USER ## `data_status`
USER 
USER Status is computed once:
USER 
USER - `complete`: every requested applicable identifier and year/component is
USER   represented;
USER - `empty`: zero rows across all coverage entries; and
USER - `partial`: anything between.
USER 
USER Reason codes are versioned and closed:
USER 
USER `identifier_not_found | years_absent | filters_matched_nothing | components_absent`
USER 
USER Coverage follows evidence order and contains complete arrays, never samples.
USER Compound results additionally name the result component. Absence is a fact;
USER cause is stated only when recorded by a source.
USER 
USER ## Grade composition
USER 
USER 1. Direct restatement → `Observed`.
USER 2. Replayable arithmetic/deterministic aggregation → `Derived`.
USER 3. Stated model plus applicable passing local backtest → `Modelled`.
USER 4. Stated model without quantified local error → `Indicative`.
USER 5. No defensible operation → `Unsupported`.
USER 6. Cap the operation grade at the weakest input grade.
USER 
USER The emitted grade records value, current ceiling, maximum achievable grade,
USER operation `rule_id`, weakest input, backtest state and adjustments. Mixed
USER responses additionally carry component grades.
USER 
USER ### Backtest policy versus state
USER 
USER Do not combine these into one enum:
USER 
USER - policy eligibility: `not_applicable | eligible | not_possible`;
USER - execution state: `blocked | ready | passed | failed`.
USER 
USER Policy changes when the capability changes. State is pinned to the registry/data
USER release and a content-addressed artifact. Any `Modelled` result requires
USER `passed` plus the artifact and applicable stratum reference.
USER 
USER VC-POC-13 is currently `Indicative`, maximum `Modelled`, eligible but blocked on
USER historical VIF vintages and realised observations. FR-32/FR-33 remain
USER `not_possible` and permanently Indicative.
USER 
USER VC-POC-14 is registered as `not_currently_supported`, current ceiling
USER `Unsupported`, maximum `Modelled`, eligible and blocked. Invocation before a
USER passing backtest returns a registry-owned `excluded_question` refusal with reason
USER code `not_yet_validated`; it is never unknown and never emitted as an Indicative
USER forecast.
USER 
USER Its horizon is one annual data step (`Calendar_Year N → N+1`), not a guaranteed
USER twelve-month operational lead. The resolved request and backtest artifact carry
USER the input reference year, `origin_as_of_date`, as-of basis, target reference or
USER census date, and actual lead time. Issuance eligibility, later outcome
USER comparability, and scoring disposition are separate recorded decisions.
USER 
USER ## Claim eligibility
USER 
USER Use per-claim state because compound answers can support different claims:
USER 
USER ```json
USER "claim_eligibility": {
USER   "trend": {
USER     "eligible": false,
USER     "decision_grade": false,
USER     "reason_codes": ["single_observation"]
USER   },
USER   "comparison": {
USER     "eligible": true,
USER     "decision_grade": true,
USER     "reason_codes": []
USER   },
USER   "position": {
USER     "eligible": true,
USER     "decision_grade": false,
USER     "reason_codes": ["thin_cohort_unverified_threshold"]
USER   }
USER }
USER ```
USER 
USER Closed v0.3 claim kinds:
USER 
USER `trend | comparison | position`
USER 
USER There is no response-global `decision_grade`: flattening would make a weak
USER component govern unrelated claims. The harness renders only claims whose
USER individual state permits them.
USER 
USER Single observations prohibit trends but remain Observed facts. A thin cohort may
USER be shown directionally while `decision_grade` is false. The unmeasured threshold
USER is recorded as advisory and cannot change grade.
USER 
USER ## Input policy
USER 
USER Every question gets a JSON Schema embedded in or referenced from the registry:
USER 
USER - `additionalProperties: false`;
USER - unconditional requirements;
USER - conditional requirements;
USER - material-to-ask inputs;
USER - structured static or dynamic defaults; and
USER - mutual-exclusion/cardinality rules.
USER 
USER The complete agreed policy is in the machine-readable draft. Material inputs
USER include market definitions, distance where applicable, peer/segment filters,
USER VC-POC-07 grades, and SA2 selection. Year ranges are defaultable. VC-POC-02
USER grades default to those actually offered in the resolved range.
USER 
USER ## Provenance
USER 
USER `provenance.source_releases` contains only releases supporting evidence in the
USER response. Every source entry must be linkable to one or more evidence indices.
USER This scoping is required before `weakest_input` can be defensible.
USER 
USER ## Replay equality
USER 
USER Within the same contract version and data release, compare the complete response
USER as semantic JSON after removing only `provenance.generated_utc`. Arrays remain
USER ordered contract data; object-key serialization order and whitespace are not
USER material.
USER 
USER ## Acceptance coverage required
USER 
USER The v0.3 suite must validate actual JSON Schemas, not only required-key sets, and
USER must include:
USER 
USER - every success fixture against the success schema;
USER - every error kind against the error schema;
USER - complete, partial and empty data status;
USER - compound-component coverage;
USER - supplied versus resolved requests and all defaults;
USER - unknown-property rejection;
USER - each conditional material input;
USER - operation grades and weakest inputs;
USER - mixed component grades for VC-POC-13;
USER - claim eligibility for single observations and thin cohorts;
USER - blocked and passed backtest states;
USER - a Modelled response rejected without a matching passing artifact;
USER - provenance restricted to used evidence; and
USER - replay equality across two runs.
USER 
USER ## Interface design (v0.3 JSON Schemas)
USER 
USER The v0.3 interface is fully specified as reviewable JSON Schemas, generated by
USER `scripts/build_poc_v0_3_schemas.py` (the single source of truth for the
USER interface) and validated by `scripts/test_poc_v0_3_schemas.py`. The v0.3 emitter
USER (`scripts/emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py`) implements this interface; the schemas and
USER emitter are reconciled and kept in agreement by the acceptance suites.
USER 
USER ### Schema map
USER 
USER | Artifact | File |
USER | --- | --- |
USER | Success envelope | `catalogue/poc_evidence_contract.v0.3.0.schema.json` |
USER | Error envelope | `catalogue/poc_evidence_error.v0.3.0.schema.json` |
USER | Input-catalog preflight | `catalogue/poc_input_catalog.v0.3.0.schema.json` |
USER | School-directory preflight | `catalogue/poc_school_directory.v0.3.0.schema.json` |
USER | Registry-owned exclusions and refusal codes | `catalogue/poc_registry_exclusions.v0.3.0.schema.json` |
USER | Per-question request schemas | `catalogue/question_schemas/v0.3.0/<QID>.request.schema.json` |
USER | Per-question `result.data` schemas | `catalogue/question_schemas/v0.3.0/<QID>.result.schema.json` |
USER | Index / materiality map | `catalogue/question_schemas/v0.3.0/_index.json` |
USER | Adapted examples and fixtures | `catalogue/question_schemas/v0.3.0/examples/`, `catalogue/poc_acceptance_fixtures.v0.3.0.json` |
USER 
USER Every request object and nested filter object sets `additionalProperties:
USER false`. Each per-question request schema carries an `x-poc` annotation block
USER (ignored by validators) recording `required`, `material`,
USER `conditional_material`, `defaultable`, `optional`, and each field's vocabulary
USER source, so the registry and harness render controls without re-deriving policy.
USER 
USER ### The semantic rule
USER 
USER The error boundary above is refined into one classification rule, enforced by
USER where each vocabulary is checked:
USER 
USER - **Invalid closed-vocabulary input → `bad_request`.** Only *static closed*
USER   vocabularies (metrics, grades, ratios, `market_definition`,
USER   `reported_enrolment_composition`, `seifa_index_type`, `seifa_measure`,
USER   `erp_sex`) and *closed-format* fields (`zone_entity_code`) are enforced with
USER   `enum`/`pattern`. A violation, an unknown property, a wrong type, a
USER   cardinality/conditional breach, or a directory ID absent from the pinned
USER   directory is mechanically detectable and repairable.
USER - **Valid input matching no facts → successful empty/partial result with
USER   `data_status`.** *Release-derived* vocabularies (`acara_sml_id`, `sa2_codes`,
USER   `lga_codes`, `erp_age`, `age_bands`, sector/type/governing-body/remoteness
USER   *values*) and *open* sets (`suburbs`, `postcodes`) are constrained by
USER   type/shape only. A well-typed value that matches no fact is never a schema
USER   failure; it is emitted as `empty` or `partial` with the coverage arrays.
USER - **Valid request impossible because a required fact is absent → `unanswerable`.**
USER   A directory-valid record lacking the selected geography or a coordinate is
USER   `unanswerable`, not `bad_request` and not an empty result.
USER 
USER `data_status.coverage` entries carry *complete arrays* for
USER `identifiers_not_found` and `years_absent` (never counts or samples), so absence
USER is enumerable; compound results additionally set `component`.
USER 
USER ### Grade, claims, provenance
USER 
USER `confidence.grade` is a structured object (value, current ceiling, maximum
USER grade, operation `rule_id`, weakest input, backtest state, adjustments, and
USER `component_grades` for mixed responses). A `Modelled` value is rejected by the
USER schema unless `backtest.status == passed` with an `artifact_reference` and
USER `stratum_reference`. `claim_eligibility` is per-claim with no response-global
USER `decision_grade`. `provenance.source_releases` entries must be linkable to
USER evidence indices.
USER 
USER ### Emitter alignment (implemented)
USER 
USER The v0.3 emitter implements the interface: it enforces `erp_sex`/`seifa_*` as
USER closed vocabularies; returns `unanswerable` for an absent-but-well-formed
USER `zone_entity_code` (VC-POC-REF-02) because there is no directory/selector
USER preflight to repair it (OD-05 settled); returns `unanswerable` for a
USER directory-valid record missing geography; emits `resolved_request`,
USER `data_status`, structured `confidence.grade`, and `claim_eligibility`; and
USER publishes current release-derived value vocabularies through `--input-catalog`
USER (`release_derived_values`) without enforcing them as request-schema enums
USER (OD-03 settled). These are recorded in the machine-readable draft under
USER `semantic_classification.emitter_alignment_implemented`.
USER 
USER ### Settled owner decisions
USER 
USER Recorded in `catalogue/poc_contract_v0.3.0.draft.json` (`owner_decisions_log`);
USER all settled by the owner:
USER 
USER - **OD-02** — the closed `refusal_reason_codes` set is accepted
USER   (`not_yet_validated`, `deferred_capability`, `out_of_scope_domain`,
USER   `prohibited_crosswalk`); CRICOS does not get its own code (CRICOS
USER   fee/competition maps to `out_of_scope_domain`).
USER - **OD-03** — closed-per-release value vocabularies (sector, school_type,
USER   governing_body, remoteness, reporting_structure, erp_age, age_bands) are NOT
USER   schema-enforced as static enums; a well-typed non-matching value yields an
USER   empty/partial result. Their current release values are published through
USER   `--input-catalog` (`release_derived_values`) so consumers can build controls.
USER - **OD-04** — `distance_km` requires a positive, finite number with no arbitrary
USER   upper bound.
USER - **OD-05** — an absent-but-well-formed `zone_entity_code` returns
USER   `unanswerable` (no directory/selector preflight to repair it).
USER - **OD-06** — VC-POC-14 uses `result_kind` `forecast`, wired through the
USER   generator/success-envelope enum, the per-question result schema, `_index.json`,
USER   and the operational registry.
USER - **OD-07** — "at least one explicit filter" (VC-POC-09/10) stays
USER   registry/emitter-enforced; the request schemas express only `minProperties >= 1`.
USER - **OD-08** — `poc_question_registry.v0.3.0.json` is retained as the operational
USER   registry carrying structured exclusions and per-question schema references.
USER 
USER ## Items deliberately outside v0.3 implementation
USER 
USER - Running the forecast backtest before its protocol and event artifact are ready.
USER - Promoting VIF without historical vintages.
USER - Automatic grade downgrades for coverage.
USER - A `School_No` → `ACARA_SML_ID` crosswalk.
USER - Any VC-POC-14 index horizon other than one annual step, or wording that
USER   represents that step as a guaranteed twelve-month operational lead.
USER ````
